{title: Valley of the Shadow}
{subtitle: Psalm 23}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want
He makes me [Gm]lie down in [Eb]green pastures
He leads me beside the [Bb]still waters
He [F]restores my [Bb]soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Though I walk through the val[Eb]ley of the shad[Bb]ow
I will fear [Eb]no evil, for you are [F]with me
[Gm]Your rod and [Eb]your staff, they comfort [Bb]me
In [Eb]the val[F]ley of the shad[Bb]ow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You prepare a [Eb]table before [Bb]me
In the presence of [Gm]my ene[Eb]mies
You anoint my head with [Bb]oil
My [F]cup over[Bb]flows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Though I walk through the val[Eb]ley of the shad[Bb]ow
I will fear no [Eb]evil, for you are [F]with me
[Gm]Your rod and [Eb]your staff, they comfort [Bb]me
In [Eb]the valley [F]of the shad[Bb]ow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I [Eb]will dwell in the [Bb]house of the Lord [Eb]forev[F]er
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
